reactor               package:AA                    R Documentation

Measured and Theoretical Temperatures of a Chemical Reactor

Description:

     The 'reactor' data frame has 20 rows and 2 columns.

     It reports the measured and theoretical temperatures in 20
     sections of a chemical reactor.

Usage:

     data(reactor)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'measured' the temperature measured in each of 20 sections of a
          chemical reactor;

     'theoretical' the theoretical temperature.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Cox, D.R. and Snell, E.J. (1981).  _Applied Statistics: principles
     and Examples_.  Chapman & Hall, London.  Example D.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Problem 37.

Examples:

     data(reactor)
     plot(measured ~ theoretical, data = reactor, xlim = c(400, 520),
          ylim = c(400, 520))
     abline(0, 1)
